// go.work makes the three modules in this repo resolve against each other from
// the local checkout during development, without a replace directive in each
// go.mod deciding it for every consumer.
//
// Replace directives are a PUBLISHED property of a module: anyone requiring
// github.com/johnewart/pyxis inherits the constraint. A workspace file affects
// only builds that see it, which is why it, not replace, is the right tool for
// "build against my checkout".
//
// This file IS committed: every path it names is inside this repo, so it means
// the same thing for everyone. A cross-repo workspace (below) should not be.
//
// The replace lines in cmd/llmd/go.mod and examples/embed/go.mod are still
// there on purpose: both are unpublished modules that must build standalone in
// CI, where go.work may be absent (and where GOWORK=off is a reasonable thing
// for a build to set).
//
// For multi-repo work — llmd alongside a consuming application — create an
// UNCOMMITTED go.work ABOVE both checkouts listing the module directories from
// each, rather than adding cross-repo replace directives here. That file is
// specific to one developer's directory layout, which is exactly why it does not
// belong in either repo.
go 1.26.0

use (
	.
	./cmd/llmd
	./examples/embed
)
